pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive direction of `wcnf_literal_spelling_alias`: `1` and `01` denote the
% same variable, as the DIMACS reading and `proof_format_overview.md` require,
% so `h 1 0` and `h -01 0` are contradictory and the empty constraint is RUP.
% This pins the canonicalized reading rather than merely a ban on non-canonical
% spellings, and it makes the WCNF front end agree with the CNF one.
f 2;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS INF INF;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
